---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout title="Coaches" current="/coaches/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Volunteer resources</p><h1>Everything coaches need.</h1><p>Compliance, practice planning, rules, and schedules for the people who make neighborhood soccer possible.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container grid two">
<article class="card"><span class="tag">Getting started</span><h2>Coach requirements</h2><p>New coaches need to complete the applicable risk management and compliance steps.</p><ul class="link-list"><li><a href="https://capitolhillsoccerclub.org/s/Fall-2025-Coach-Compliance-Instructions-for-New-Coaches.docx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Existing coach compliance instructions</a></li><li><a href="https://www.sysa.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SYSA coaching resources</a></li></ul><p class="fineprint">The existing instructions are labeled 2025; confirm current requirements with SYSA.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="tag">On the field</span><h2>Schedules & rules</h2><p>Find practice and game information, along with league rules.</p><ul class="link-list"><li><a href="/schedules/">Schedules and fields</a></li><li><a href="https://www.sysa.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">League rules and guidance</a></li></ul></article>
<article class="card"><span class="tag">Practice planning</span><h2>Training plans</h2><p>The current club site publishes week-by-week training plans for U9–U10 and U11+ coaches.</p><ul class="link-list"><li><a href="https://capitolhillsoccerclub.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Week 1 and Week 3 plans (existing site)</a></li><li><a href="https://capitolhillsoccerclub.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Week 5 plans (existing site)</a></li></ul><p class="fineprint">Direct source-file links should be migrated before launch.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="tag">Get involved</span><h2>Interested in coaching?</h2><p>Volunteer coaches are essential to recreational youth soccer. Reach out to learn how to help.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:info@caphillsoccer.org?subject=Coaching%20volunteer">Ask about coaching ↗</a></article>
</div></section>
</SiteLayout>
